#!/opt/bin/perl

=encoding utf8

=head1 NAME

mcp-webbrowser - expose opted-in browser tabs to MCP

=head1 SYNOPSIS

   mcp-webbrowser --stdio
   mcp-webbrowser --print-url
   mcp-webbrowser --stdio --bind 127.0.0.1:31741
   mcp-webbrowser --connect http://host:port/TOKEN/browser

=head1 DESCRIPTION

The companion userscript lets you explicitly grant an MCP client access to
individual browser tabs. Only opted-in tabs connect to this broker over
WebSocket; MCP clients can then discover those tabs, execute JavaScript in
their page context and add DOM elements. Code can inspect or change the
page, including logged-in content and forms, and cause side effects. Treat
allowing a tab as giving the MCP client access to that page, not merely its
URL or title. The broker still applies its own MCP permission rules.

This executable is the broker, not a browser extension. The userscript
handles per-tab authorization and page execution. The broker cannot see
unapproved tabs merely because the userscript is installed.

The HTTP/WebSocket listener stays active alongside MCP stdio or an outgoing
C<--connect>. Listener configuration, token derivation and URL discovery follow
C<mcp-vim>. Tokens authenticate both MCP HTTP and browser WebSocket connections.
Keep the broker URL private. The userscript accepts the C<http://> URL printed
by C<mcp-webbrowser --print-url>, converts it to WebSocket internally and
appends its own opaque per-tab target ID.

=head1 USERSCRIPT INSTALLATION AND USE

The self-contained userscript is C<webbrowser/mcp-webbrowser.user.js> in the
AnyEvent::MCP source distribution. Installing the Perl distribution does
not install it in a browser. Install a userscript manager first; see the
L<ScriptCat installation guide|https://docs.scriptcat.org/en/docs/use/use/>.
B<ScriptCat on Chromium and Firefox has been tested> (Firefox 153 on Linux,
including page execution, DOM insertion and navigation). ScriptCat is available
for Chrome, Edge and Firefox. Tampermonkey
provides the required C<GM_getTab>/C<GM_saveTab> APIs and may work, but
has not been tested with this userscript. Other managers are unverified.

Install the source-distribution file through your userscript manager, or
open the published userscript URL in the browser and install it there:

   https://dist.schmorp.de/mcp-webbrowser/1/mcp-webbrowser.user.js

The C</1/> is the major version of the private browser/broker protocol, not
the MCP protocol or Perl distribution version. The published script declares
that URL for installation and automatic updates; updates depend on the
userscript manager. The source file contains the entire userscript and
needs no external JavaScript import.

Start the broker (directly or through your MCP client/multibroker) and obtain
its listener URL with:

   mcp-webbrowser --stdio
   mcp-webbrowser --print-url

The second command prints the URL and exits; run it with the same service
name and configuration as the running broker. It does not launch a second
listener. On a page you want to expose, select B<Allow MCP access to this
tab> from the userscript menu. The first time, enter the full URL printed
by C<--print-url> when prompted. Do not append a tab name or convert
C<http> to C<ws> yourself. The URL is remembered across tabs; the grant is
per tab, not per website. Pages remain unexposed until explicitly allowed,
and the menu on an unapproved tab contains only the Allow command.

When allowed, the menu offers B<Disconnect MCP access to this tab>, the
broker URL configuration and independent toggles for a tab-title indicator
and a notification in the page when switching to that tab. Both indicators
are enabled by default. The title prefix is C<[○MCP]> while connecting,
C<[●MCP]> when connected and C<[⊗MCP]> after prolonged failure. The toast
shows the same status and disappears shortly after a successful connection.
The indicator prefix is omitted from titles reported to the broker.
The permission remains granted during temporary disconnections and normally
survives navigation or reload until explicitly revoked.

If a tab does not connect, check that the broker is running and its URL is
correct. Depending on browser settings, you may also need to allow the page
to access a local-loopback or local-network address; browser permission
blocking can look like a WebSocket failure. The title and toast indicators
report connectivity, not a trustworthy security boundary.

B<Note:> ScriptCat currently loses the saved per-tab permission when
Chromium replaces a discarded tab. After such a discard and restoration,
you must choose Allow again. This is tracked in
L<https://github.com/scriptscat/scriptcat/issues/1791>.

=head1 FIRST TOOL CALL

After allowing a tab, ask your assistant:

   Call tabs and show the connected tabs. On one of them, execute
   document.title and show its result.

Use a C<target> returned by C<tabs> for the C<execute> call. Listing
requires C<read> permission; even this simple JavaScript expression needs
C<exec> permission, because execution has full page authority. The
tool returns an object containing C<value>; there is no read-only mode.

With a multibroker prefix C<browser>, the tools are C<browser.tabs>
and C<browser.execute>. If no tab is listed, confirm that the userscript
was allowed B<on that tab> and that its indicator shows a connection.
Installing the userscript does not grant access to any tabs.
An execution error or timeout does not prove that nothing happened;
do not blindly retry JavaScript that changes page state.

=head1 TOOLS

=over

=item tabs

Return C<{tabs: [...]}> with each connected tab's C<target>, current document
C<instance_id>, integer C<revision>, and client-reported C<url> and C<title>.
The revision starts at 1 and advances on document replacement, not on an
ordinary WebSocket reconnect or a same-document navigation. Disconnected tab
identities are retained for up to 30 seconds. This is cached registration
metadata, not a fresh DOM inspection. Requires C<read> permission.

=item execute

Run C<code> on C<target>. Optional C<instance_id> and C<revision> from C<tabs>
reject a replaced document before dispatch. C<timeout> defaults to 30 seconds
and can be 1..300 seconds. With C<navigate> false (the default), the browser
awaits the evaluation result. Results are C<{value: JSON_VALUE}>; exceptions
become tool errors.
Replies default to a 16 KiB UTF-8 JSON limit; C<max_bytes> can raise the
limit to 2 MiB (minimum 1024 bytes). The size includes the JSON envelope.
Oversized results yield an error instead of truncating JSON or disconnecting
the browser. Code has already executed when the size error is returned;
do not blindly retry commands with side effects.

With C<navigate> true, the broker sends the command, awaits the browser's
C<ready> message, and sends C<proceed> before the browser evaluates it.
The broker then waits for either a new document registering on the same tab
or an observed same-document navigation. The result has C<navigation> equal
to C<document> or C<same-document>, the resulting C<revision>, and reported
URL/title. If neither completion is observed before the timeout, it returns
C<navigation: "timeout"> with a reason, current revision and available metadata.
Timeout does not imply that the command was not executed; no automatic retry
is attempted. One navigation operation at a time is allowed per tab.

The browser client injects C<code> as body of C<async () =E<gt> CODE>
in the page's JavaScript world. Supply only CODE, not the arrow-function
wrapper. For example, C<({title: document.title})> returns an object;
C<async () =E<gt> ({title: document.title})> returns a function and is
rejected as a non-JSON result. Single expression yields its value without
C<return>; braced function body needs explicit C<return> for multiple
statements.
C<await> works inside either form. Declarations in the body do not persist
between calls unless assigned to page globals. Results are awaited. This
does not use C<eval> or C<Function>. Syntax errors can prevent the injected
script from starting; a temporary page-world error listener tries to return
the native syntax-error message, otherwise the client reports an injection
failure. Source injection is serialized until each script acknowledges
successful compilation or fails; asynchronous execution thereafter may
overlap. Code has full page-context authority, with no read-only evaluation
mode or sandbox claim.

Cancellation and timeout send a best-effort cancel message. They cannot undo
already executed code or guarantee that JavaScript stops. Disconnect fails
ordinary pending calls without replaying them. A navigation request persists
across disconnects and may complete on the next document's registration.
Concurrent human navigation can satisfy a pending request; success reports
observation, not proof that the submitted code caused the navigation.

=item add-element

Insert an element through the userscript's C<GM_addElement> in the content
sandbox. This can bypass page CSP for stylesheets and scripts. Required
C<target> and C<tag>; optional C<parent> is a document CSS selector
(default: document root). C<attributes> contains HTML attribute strings,
while C<properties> contains DOM property values, such as C<textContent>
or C<innerHTML>. Properties are supplied during element creation; attributes
are set explicitly as well. An unsuccessful selector or insertion is an error.
The result is C<{value: {tag: TAG, id: ID_OR_NULL}}> and does not assert that
the caller's C<id> is unique. No automatic ID or registry is maintained: give
elements a distinctive C<id> or C<data-*> attribute when later page-context
C<execute> calls need to modify or remove them. Uses C<exec> permission and
supports the same optional C<instance_id> and C<revision> guards as C<execute>.

=back

=head1 PERMISSIONS

The default rule file is C<~/.config/anyevent-mcp/rules/webbrowser-default.ini>,
under C<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME> when set. C<--name NAME> replaces C<default>.
C<read> covers tab discovery; C<exec> covers arbitrary JavaScript.

Exec prompts offer this exact code in this target, any code in this target,
or any code in all targets. Saved target grants also cover future tabs using
the same target name. Client-reported URLs and titles are display information,
not verified origin identities or saved permission scopes.
C<--ask> selects the same helper, tty, yad, mcp or auto modes as other servers.

=head1 OPTIONS

Common server options: L<AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Simple/mcp_getoptions>.
The HTTP/WebSocket listener remains active under C<--stdio> or C<--connect>.
C<--tool-help> lists registered tools and arguments without listening.
For example, C<--auto-allow '*,*'> approves discovery and JavaScript
execution in explicitly opted-in tabs; page code then has full authority.

=over

=item --ask MODE

Permission prompts: C<helper> (default), C<tty>, C<yad>, C<mcp> or
C<auto>. tty/yad force local interface; mcp delegates to client,
auto prefers native elicitation when offered. See L</PERMISSIONS>.

=back

=head1 BROWSER PROTOCOL

WebSocket authentication happens at C</TOKEN/TARGET>. C<TARGET> is one
percent-encoded path component. Before ordinary messages, send:

   ["mcp-webbrowser", 1, 0, INSTANCE_ID, {"url": URL, "title": TITLE}]

C<INSTANCE_ID> identifies one loaded document. Keep it across reconnects of that
document and change it on navigation/reload. The private browser protocol is
1.0, independent of MCP and the old xpcse browser-transfer protocol.
The broker answers C<["welcome", TARGET, INSTANCE_ID, REVISION]>.
The requested target represents a browser tab: a different document with the
same target replaces its previous connection and increments the revision.
Reconnecting the same document retains that revision. A disconnected tab's
identity expires after 30 seconds with no pending navigation. No page is
exposed before a valid hello.

A tab session starts on first hello, remains active across temporary socket
disconnects and document replacements, and finishes on an explicit C<quit>,
after 30 seconds of inactivity, or when the broker stops. Session start
and finish are logged at C<info>; ordinary socket connection and disconnection
events are logged at C<trace>. Revision and request IDs are transmitted as
JSON numbers, even when Perl string operations have touched those scalars.
Approved JavaScript is logged at C<trace> when dispatched for ordinary evaluation,
or when C<proceed> is sent for navigation (never during the permission prompt).

Broker to browser:

   ["call", ID, "execute", {"code": CODE, "max_bytes": BYTES}]
   ["call", ID, "navigate", {"code": CODE, "max_bytes": BYTES}]
   ["call", ID, "add_element", {"tag": TAG, "parent": SELECTOR, "attributes": ATTRS, "properties": PROPS}]
   ["proceed", ID]
   ["cancel", ID]

Browser to broker:

   ["reply", ID, true, JSON_VALUE]
   ["reply", ID, false, ERROR_STRING]
   ["ready", ID]
   ["navigated", ID, {"url": URL, "title": TITLE}]
   ["state", {"url": URL, "title": TITLE}]
   ["quit"]

The browser replies C<ready> to a C<navigate> call without evaluating it.
Only C<proceed> starts evaluation. C<navigated> reports a completed
same-document navigation; a different document's hello is the other
completion path. C<reply> with C<false> can report an evaluation failure.
Only JSON values cross the wire; undefined becomes null. Errors are strings.
Late replies after cancellation are ignored. State updates replace cached
metadata. Malformed messages close the connection with status 1002.
The initial hello has a 15-second deadline; a silent connection is closed.

The distributed userscript evaluates in the page's JavaScript world via an
injected script and returns serialized results through DOM events. Its
Navigation API listener is installed in that same world. The broker cannot
authenticate page-reported values or infer application-rendering readiness
from navigation success. The userscript retries disconnected WebSockets;
it has no event subscriptions or separate SPA revision counter.

=cut

use common::sense;
use AnyEvent ();
use AnyEvent::Socket ();
use AnyEvent::Handle ();
use AnyEvent::MCP ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Config ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Server::HTTP ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Server::JSONL ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Permissions ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Toolset ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Simple qw(mcp_getoptions mcp_tool_help mcp_log mcp_log_request);
use AnyEvent::WebSocket::Server ();
use AnyEvent::WebSocket::Message ();
use JSON::XS ();
use Socket ();
use Scalar::Util qw(weaken);

my $options = mcp_getoptions ({
   usage => "Usage: mcp-webbrowser [OPTION]...\n",
   path => "/",
   description => "Expose connected browser tabs to MCP; HTTP/WebSocket stays active with stdio or --connect.",
   options => [["--ask MODE", "Ask via helper (default), tty, yad, mcp, or auto"]],
   examples => "  mcp-webbrowser --auto-allow '*,*' # all actions in opted-in tabs",
}, "ask=s" => \my $ask);
@ARGV and die "Unexpected arguments\n";
my $name = $options->{name};
my $connect = $options->{connect};
my $stdio = $options->{stdio} || !defined $connect && $ENV{PERL_ANYEVENT_MCP_MULTIBROKER_PROTOCOL} eq "stdio";
!($stdio && defined $connect) or die "Cannot combine --stdio and --connect\n";

my $config = AnyEvent::MCP::Config->global;
my %http = $config->http_settings ($name, $options->{bind});
$http{tokens} = $options->{tokens} if $options->{tokens};
my %token = map { $_ => 1 } @{$http{tokens}};
my $json = JSON::XS->new->utf8->max_depth (64);
my (%connections, %pages, %tabs);
my $done = AE::cv;

my $permissions = AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Permissions->new (
   name => "webbrowser-$name",
   actions => {
      read => "List connected browser tabs and their reported metadata",
      exec => "Execute arbitrary JavaScript in a connected browser page",
   },
   (defined $ask ? (ask => $ask) : ()),
   auto_rules => [@{$options->{auto_rules} || []},
      $config->auto_rules ($name)],
);

sub page_label {
   my ($state) = @_;

   my ($title, $url) = @{$state}{qw(title url)};
   s/[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/ /g for $title, $url;

   (length $title ? substr ($title, 0, 80) . " - " : "")
      . substr ($url, 0, 160)
}

sub code_preview {
   my ($code, $limit) = @_;

   $limit //= 160;
   my $short = substr ($code, 0, $limit);
   $short .= "..." if length $code > $limit;
   $json->encode ($short)
}

sub url_preview {
   my $url = shift;

   $url =~ s/[?#].*//s;
   $url =~ s{(://)[^/]*@}{$1};
   $url =~ s/[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/ /g;
   my $short = substr ($url, 0, 64);
   $short .= "..." if length $url > 64;
   $json->encode ($short)
}

sub permission {
   my ($req, $action, $target, $code) = @_;

   my $subject = "tabs";
   my @subjects = ({ label => "the list of connected browser tabs", subject => $subject });

   if (defined $target) {
      my $label = $target;
      if (my $page = $pages{$target}) {
         $label = page_label ($page->{state}) . " (tab " . substr ($target, 0, 8) . ")";
      }

      my $coder = JSON::XS->new->allow_nonref;
      my $prefix = "execute:" . $coder->encode ($target) . ":";
      $subject = $prefix . $coder->encode ($code);
      @subjects = (
         { label => "this exact code in page '$label'", subject => $subject },
         { label => "any JavaScript in page '$label'", subject => "^" . (quotemeta $prefix) },
         { label => "any JavaScript in all browser tabs, including future connections", subject => "^" },
      );
      $target = $label;
   }

   $req->require_permission ({
      tool => $req->{tool}, action => $action,
      subject => $subject, subjects => \@subjects, sandbox_grants => [],
      reason => defined $target ? "Execute JavaScript in '$target'\n\n$code" : "List connected browser tabs",
   });
}

sub send_message {
   my ($page, $message) = @_;

   $page->{conn}->send (AnyEvent::WebSocket::Message->new (opcode => 1, body => $json->encode ($message)));
}

sub finish_call {
   my ($page, $id, $success, $value) = @_;

   my $entry = delete $page->{pending}{$id} or return;
   my $req = $entry->{request};
   return if $req->{finished};

   $success ? $req->result ({ value => $value }) : $req->error ($value)
}

sub finish_tab {
   my ($tab, $reason) = @_;

   return unless $tabs{$tab->{requested}} && $tabs{$tab->{requested}} == $tab;
   delete $tab->{expiry};
   delete $tabs{$tab->{requested}};
   mcp_log "$tab->{requested}: session finished ($reason)";
}

sub expire_tab {
   my ($tab) = @_;

   delete $tab->{expiry};
   return if $tab->{page} || $tab->{navigation};

   $tab->{expiry} = AE::timer 30, 0, sub {
      finish_tab $tab, "inactive for 30s"
         unless $tab->{page} || $tab->{navigation};
   };
}

sub finish_navigation {
   my ($tab, $kind, $reason) = @_;

   my $entry = delete $tab->{navigation} or return;
   delete $entry->{timer};
   my $req = $entry->{request};
   return if $req->{finished};

   my $page = $tab->{page};
   $req->result ({
      navigation => $kind,
      revision   => $tab->{revision}*1,
      ($page ? (%{$page->{state}}) : ()),
      (defined $reason ? (reason => $reason) : ()),
   });

   expire_tab $tab unless $page;
}

sub close_page {
   my ($page, $code, $reason) = @_;

   delete $connections{$page+0} or return;
   delete $pages{$page->{target}} if defined $page->{target} && $pages{$page->{target}} == $page;
   delete $page->{hello_timer};

   if (my $tab = $page->{tab}) {
      delete $tab->{page} if $tab->{page} == $page;
      expire_tab $tab;
   }

   finish_call $page, $_, 0, $reason for keys %{$page->{pending}};
   $page->{conn}->close ($code, $reason);
   if (defined $page->{target}) {
      mcp_log "$page->{target}: disconnected ($reason)";
   } else {
      AE::log trace => "Browser WebSocket disconnected before hello ($reason)";
   }
}

sub valid_state {
   my ($state) = @_;

   ref $state eq "HASH" && defined $state->{url} && !ref $state->{url}
      && defined $state->{title} && !ref $state->{title}
}

sub receive_message {
   my ($page, $packet) = @_;

   ref $packet eq "ARRAY" && @$packet && defined $packet->[0] && !ref $packet->[0]
      or die "Invalid browser message\n";

   unless (defined $page->{target}) {
      @$packet == 5 && $packet->[0] eq "mcp-webbrowser"
         && defined $packet->[1] && !ref $packet->[1] && $packet->[1] eq "1"
         && defined $packet->[2] && !ref $packet->[2] && $packet->[2] eq "0"
         && defined $packet->[3] && !ref $packet->[3] && length $packet->[3]
         && valid_state ($packet->[4])
         or die "Invalid browser hello\n";

      my $new = !exists $tabs{$page->{requested}};
      my $tab = $tabs{$page->{requested}} ||= {
         requested => $page->{requested}, revision => 0,
      };
      my $different = !defined $tab->{instance_id} || $tab->{instance_id} ne $packet->[3];
      close_page $tab->{page}, 1000, "Page connection replaced" if $tab->{page};
      delete $tab->{expiry};

      ++$tab->{revision} if $different;
      $tab->{instance_id} = $packet->[3];
      @$page{qw(target instance_id state tab)} = ($page->{requested}, $packet->[3], $packet->[4], $tab);
      $tab->{page} = $page;
      delete $page->{hello_timer};
      $pages{$page->{target}} = $page;
      send_message $page, ["welcome", $page->{target}, $page->{instance_id}, $tab->{revision}*1];

      if ($different && $tab->{navigation} && $tab->{navigation}{phase} eq "proceed") {
         finish_navigation $tab, "document";
      }

      mcp_log "$page->{target}: session started (" . url_preview ($page->{state}{url}) . ")" if $new;
      mcp_log "$page->{target}: connected (revision $tab->{revision})"
         unless $new;
      return
   }

   my $type = $packet->[0];

   if ($type eq "reply") {
      @$packet == 4 && defined $packet->[1] && !ref $packet->[1] && $packet->[1] =~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/
         && defined $packet->[2] && ($packet->[2] eq "0" || $packet->[2] eq "1")
         && ($packet->[2] || defined $packet->[3] && !ref $packet->[3])
         or die "Invalid browser reply\n";
      my $entry = $page->{tab}{navigation};
      if ($entry && $entry->{page} == $page && $entry->{id} == $packet->[1]) {
         if (!$packet->[2]) {
            delete $page->{tab}{navigation};
            delete $entry->{timer};
            $entry->{request}->error ($packet->[3]) unless $entry->{request}{finished};
         }
      } else {
         finish_call $page, @$packet[1, 2, 3];
      }
   } elsif ($type eq "ready") {
      @$packet == 2 && defined $packet->[1] && !ref $packet->[1]
         && $packet->[1] =~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/ or die "Invalid navigation acknowledgement\n";

      my $entry = $page->{tab}{navigation};
      if ($entry && $entry->{page} == $page && $entry->{id} == $packet->[1]
          && $entry->{phase} eq "ready") {
         $entry->{phase} = "proceed";
         AE::log trace => "webbrowser navigate $page->{target} #$entry->{id}: " . code_preview ($entry->{code});
         send_message $page, ["proceed", $packet->[1]*1];
      }
   } elsif ($type eq "navigated") {
      @$packet == 3 && defined $packet->[1] && !ref $packet->[1]
         && $packet->[1] =~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/ && valid_state ($packet->[2])
         or die "Invalid navigation result\n";

      my $entry = $page->{tab}{navigation};
      if ($entry && $entry->{page} == $page && $entry->{id} == $packet->[1]
          && $entry->{phase} eq "proceed") {
         $page->{state} = $packet->[2];
         finish_navigation $page->{tab}, "same-document";
      }
   } elsif ($type eq "state") {
      @$packet == 2 && valid_state ($packet->[1]) or die "Invalid browser state\n";
      $page->{state} = $packet->[1];
   } elsif ($type eq "quit") {
      @$packet == 1 or die "Invalid browser quit\n";
      close_page $page, 1000, "Page disconnected";
      finish_tab $page->{tab}, "disabled"
         if $page->{tab} && !$page->{tab}{navigation};
   } else {
      die "Unknown browser message\n";
   }
}

sub accept_browser {
   my ($fh) = @_;

   my $requested;
   my $ws = AnyEvent::WebSocket::Server->new (
      max_payload_size => 16 * 1024 * 1024,
      handshake => sub {
         my ($req, $res) = @_;
         my ($cookie, $target) = $req->{resource_name} =~ m{\A/([^/]+)/([^/?#]+)\z};
         defined $cookie && $token{$cookie} or return;
         $target =~ /%(?![0-9a-fA-F]{2})/ and return;
         $target =~ s/%([0-9a-fA-F]{2})/chr hex $1/ge;
         utf8::decode $target or return;
         length $target && $target !~ /\0/ or return;
         $requested = $target;

         $res
      },
   );
   $ws->establish ($fh)->cb (sub {
      my $conn = eval { $_[0]->recv };
      unless ($conn) {
         AE::log warn => "Browser WebSocket establishment failed: " . ($@ || "no connection");
         return;
      }

      my $page = { conn => $conn, requested => $requested, pending => {}, rpcid => 0 };
      $connections{$page+0} = $page;
      weaken (my $weak = $page);
      $conn->on (finish => sub { close_page $weak, 1000, "Page disconnected" if $weak });
      $conn->on (each_message => sub {
         return unless $weak && exists $connections{$weak+0};
         my $ok = eval {
            $_[1]->opcode == 1 or die "Browser messages must be text\n";
            receive_message $weak, $json->decode ($_[1]->body);
            1
         };
         unless ($ok) {
            AE::log warn => "Browser protocol error: $@";
            close_page $weak, 1002, "Invalid browser protocol";
         }
      });
      $page->{hello_timer} = AE::timer 15, 0, sub {
         close_page $weak, 1002, "Browser hello timed out" if $weak;
      };
   });
}

my $toolset = AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Toolset->new;
$toolset->tool (tabs => "List connected tabs; metadata client-reported.",
   { type => "object", properties => {}, additionalProperties => JSON::XS::false },
   sub {
      my ($req) = @_;
      permission $req, "read";
      AE::log debug => "webbrowser tabs";
      $req->result ({ tabs => [map {
         my $page = $pages{$_};
         +{ %{$page->{state}}, target => $_, instance_id => $page->{instance_id},
            revision => $page->{tab}{revision}*1 }
      } sort keys %pages] });
   },
);
$toolset->tool (execute => "Page JS: CODE becomes body of async () => CODE; supply CODE, not arrow-function wrapper. "
      . "Example: ({title: document.title}); NOT async () => ({title: document.title}) (returns function, rejected). "
      . "Single expression returns implicitly; { ... } body needs explicit return; await works. "
      . "UTF-8 JSON reply max_bytes=16384 (16 KiB) default, max 2097152 (2 MiB). Oversize errors after execution; no truncation. "
      . "navigate=true: acknowledge before execution, "
      . "then wait for new document or observed same-document navigation. "
      . "Revision/instance guards reject replaced documents.",
   {
      type => "object",
      properties => {
         target => { type => "string", minLength => 1 },
         code => { type => "string", description => "Expression or { ... } body for async () => CODE. Do not include async () => wrapper." },
         instance_id => { type => "string", minLength => 1 },
         revision => { type => "integer", minimum => 1 },
         navigate => { type => "boolean", default => JSON::XS::false },
         max_bytes => { type => "integer", minimum => 1024, maximum => 2 * 1024 * 1024, default => 16 * 1024 },
         timeout => { type => "number", minimum => 1, maximum => 300, default => 30 },
      },
      required => ["target", "code"], additionalProperties => JSON::XS::false,
   },
   sub {
      my ($req, $args) = @_;

      my $page = $pages{$args->{target}} or die "Browser page is not connected\n";
      !defined $args->{instance_id} || $args->{instance_id} eq $page->{instance_id}
         or die "Browser document instance changed\n";
      !defined $args->{revision} || $args->{revision} == $page->{tab}{revision}
         or die "Browser document revision changed (now $page->{tab}{revision})\n";
      !$page->{tab}{navigation} or die "Navigation already in progress for this tab\n";
      permission $req, exec => $args->{target}, $args->{code};

      AE::log debug => "webbrowser " . ($args->{navigate} ? "navigate " : "execute ")
         . $json->encode ($args->{target}) . " " . url_preview ($page->{state}{url})
         . " " . code_preview ($args->{code}, 20);

      $pages{$args->{target}} && $pages{$args->{target}} == $page
         or die "Browser document changed while permission was pending\n";

      my $id = ++$page->{rpcid};
      if ($args->{navigate}) {
         my $tab = $page->{tab};
         my $entry = $tab->{navigation} = {
            request => $req, page => $page, id => $id, phase => "ready", code => $args->{code},
         };
         $entry->{timer} = AE::timer $args->{timeout} // 30, 0, sub {
            return unless $tab->{navigation} && $tab->{navigation} == $entry;
            if ($entry->{phase} eq "proceed") {
               send_message $entry->{page}, ["cancel", $id*1] if $tab->{page} && $tab->{page} == $entry->{page};
               finish_navigation $tab, "timeout", "No completed navigation was observed before timeout";
            } else {
               delete $tab->{navigation};
               send_message $page, ["cancel", $id*1] if $tab->{page} && $tab->{page} == $page;
               $req->error ("Browser did not acknowledge navigation") unless $req->{finished};
               expire_tab $tab unless $tab->{page};
            }
         };
         $req->{on_cancel} = sub {
            return unless $tab->{navigation} && $tab->{navigation} == $entry;
            delete $tab->{navigation};
            delete $entry->{timer};
            send_message $page, ["cancel", $id*1] if $tab->{page} && $tab->{page} == $page;
            expire_tab $tab unless $tab->{page};
         };
         send_message $page, ["call", $id*1, "navigate", { code => $args->{code}, max_bytes => $args->{max_bytes} // 16 * 1024 }];
         return;
      }

      my $entry = $page->{pending}{$id} = { request => $req };
      weaken (my $weak = $page);
      $entry->{timer} = AE::timer $args->{timeout} // 30, 0, sub {
         return unless $weak && exists $weak->{pending}{$id};
         send_message $weak, ["cancel", $id*1];
         finish_call $weak, $id, 0, "Browser execution timed out";
      };
      $req->{on_cancel} = sub {
         return unless $weak && delete $weak->{pending}{$id};
         send_message $weak, ["cancel", $id*1];
      };
      AE::log trace => "webbrowser execute $args->{target} #$id: " . code_preview ($args->{code});
      send_message $page, ["call", $id*1, "execute", { code => $args->{code}, max_bytes => $args->{max_bytes} // 16 * 1024 }];
   },
);
$toolset->tool (add_element => "Insert DOM element via userscript GM_addElement; style/script bypass page CSP. "
      . "Set HTML attributes via attributes; DOM properties (textContent/innerHTML) via properties. "
      . "parent: CSS selector; default document.documentElement. "
      . "Set distinctive id or data-* to find/edit/remove later via execute. "
      . "No automatic ID/registry.",
   {
      type => "object",
      properties => {
         target => { type => "string", minLength => 1 },
         tag => { type => "string", minLength => 1 },
         parent => { type => "string", minLength => 1 },
         attributes => { type => "object", additionalProperties => { type => "string" } },
         properties => { type => "object", additionalProperties => JSON::XS::true },
         instance_id => { type => "string", minLength => 1 },
         revision => { type => "integer", minimum => 1 },
      },
      required => ["target", "tag"], additionalProperties => JSON::XS::false,
   },
   sub {
      my ($req, $args) = @_;

      my $page = $pages{$args->{target}} or die "Browser page is not connected\n";
      !defined $args->{instance_id} || $args->{instance_id} eq $page->{instance_id}
         or die "Browser document instance changed\n";
      !defined $args->{revision} || $args->{revision} == $page->{tab}{revision}
         or die "Browser document revision changed (now $page->{tab}{revision})\n";
      !$page->{tab}{navigation} or die "Navigation already in progress for this tab\n";
      permission $req, exec => $args->{target}, "GM_addElement " . $json->encode ($args);
      $pages{$args->{target}} && $pages{$args->{target}} == $page
         or die "Browser document changed while permission was pending\n";

      my $id = ++$page->{rpcid};
      my $entry = $page->{pending}{$id} = { request => $req };
      weaken (my $weak = $page);
      $entry->{timer} = AE::timer 30, 0, sub {
         return unless $weak && exists $weak->{pending}{$id};
         send_message $weak, ["cancel", $id*1];
         finish_call $weak, $id, 0, "Browser add_element timed out";
      };
      $req->{on_cancel} = sub {
         return unless $weak && delete $weak->{pending}{$id};
         send_message $weak, ["cancel", $id*1];
      };
      AE::log debug => "webbrowser add_element $args->{target}: " . $json->encode ($args->{tag});
      send_message $page, ["call", $id*1, "add_element", {
         map { exists $args->{$_} ? ($_ => $args->{$_}) : () } qw(tag parent attributes properties)
      }];
   },
);

mcp_tool_help ($options->{tool_help}, $toolset);

my $custom_instructions = $options->{custom_instructions}
   // $config->{section}{"instance $name"}{custom_instructions}
   // $config->{section}{"program " . AnyEvent::MCP::Config::program_name ()}{custom_instructions};
my %server = (
   server_info => { name => "mcp-webbrowser", version => "0" },
   auto_instructions  => 1,
   short_instructions => "Inspect connected tabs; run page JavaScript. Discover tools.",
   (defined $custom_instructions ? (custom_instructions => $custom_instructions) : ()),
   instructions => "Tabs have stable targets/document revisions. "
      . "Use tabs for current revision. execute runs async () => CODE in page; "
      . "expression returns implicitly; { ... } body needs return; parenthesize object literals. "
      . "navigate=true acknowledges before evaluation; waits for new document or SPA navigation. "
      . "Navigation result: document, same-document, timeout. Execution may have happened even on timeout; never retried. "
      . "Guard later calls with revision; metadata client-reported.",
   toolsets => [$toolset], permissions => $permissions,
   on_request => \&mcp_log_request,
   on_error => sub { AE::log info => "mcp-tool $_[1]{tool}: $_[2]" },
);
my $http = AnyEvent::MCP::Server::HTTP->new (%server, %http, path => "/");
my $stream;

if (defined $connect) {
   require AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Connect;
   $stream = AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Connect->new (
      %server, connect => $connect, on_close => sub { $done->send },
   );
   $stream->start;
} elsif ($stdio) {
   binmode STDIN;
   binmode STDOUT;
   $stream = AnyEvent::MCP::Server::JSONL->new (
      %server, on_connection_close => sub { $done->send },
   );
   $stream->accept (\*STDIN, \*STDOUT);
}

my $listener = AnyEvent::Socket::tcp_server $http{host}, $http{port}, sub {
   my ($fh) = @_ or return;
   my $watcher; $watcher = AE::io $fh, 0, sub {
      undef $watcher;
      defined recv $fh, my $magic, 1, Socket::MSG_PEEK or return;
      if ($magic eq "G") {
         accept_browser $fh;
      } else {
         $http->accept ($fh);
      }
   };
};
my @signals = map { AE::signal $_, sub { $done->send } } qw(INT TERM);
$done->recv;
undef $listener;
close_page $_, 1000, "Browser broker stopped" for values %connections;
finish_tab $_, "broker stopped" for values %tabs;
$stream->close if $stream;
$http->close;
